# HTML pages

## Relative paths

- Root `index.html`: `css/…`, `js/…`, `pages/…`, `assets/…`, `public/…`
- Under `pages/`: `../css/…`, `../js/…`, sibling `*.html`, `../assets/…`
- Under `pages/case-studies/` or `pages/insights/`: `../../css/…`, `../../js/…`, `../../assets/…`, `../../public/…`; sibling pages in the same folder; other top-level pages via `../services.html`, etc. Prefer Home/logo → `../../index.html` (canonical `/`), not `homepage.html`.
- Under `pages/`: Home/logo → `../index.html`.

Wrong paths are a common production break. Verify root, `pages/*`, and nested `pages/*/*` after moves.

## Shared chrome

Header and footer are **generated** from `scripts/chrome/` by `python3 scripts/sync-chrome.py` — edit the templates, never the pages. The floating contact block is still per-page.

Nav order: Home · Services · Products · Resources (dropdown: Case Studies, Insights) · About · Contact.

Homepage content lives only in `index.html`; `pages/homepage.html` is a noindex redirect stub.

## Forms (contact + newsletter)

Preserve Contact FormSubmit fields (`_subject`, `_next`, `_template`, `_autoresponse`) and the thank-you hash flow (`#thank-you`) unless explicitly changing conversion UX.

Insights newsletter uses a **separate** FormSubmit form (same `hello@prodatalytics.com`, different `_subject` / `_next` → `#newsletter-thanks`). Do not alter Contact form fields when editing the newsletter.

Homepage floating form posts via FormSubmit in `js/common.js` (submit UX only; do not `preventDefault` the FormSubmit POST).

## Insights content

- Articles: `pages/insights/<slug>.html` + row in `data/insights-index.json` (search via `js/insights.js`)
- Case studies: `pages/case-studies/<slug>.html` + listing card on `pages/case-studies/index.html`
- Briefs / series templates: `docs/content-templates.md`

## SEO / meta

Keep per-page `title`, description, and OG/Twitter tags accurate. Prefer `https://www.prodatalytics.com/…` for canonical/OG URLs when touching them.

## Do not casually reintroduce

Removed marketing blocks (testimonials, ROI strips, “trusted by”) — only with product intent. See README future items. Selected work / case studies are intentional and allowed.
